    q: 'Between 1508 and 1512, Michelangelo painted the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel in Rome, a commission that came from Pope Julius II. ----. Some accounts suggest that he accepted the work only reluctantly and would rather have spent those years on marble. Once he had begun, however, he devoted himself to the project, covering the vast vault with frescoes while working from a high wooden platform. The finished ceiling soon came to be seen as one of the great achievements of the age.',
